  "nl_text": "The rschema_0446 database is designed to manage data related to crop growth and monitoring. At its core, it contains information about users, who are identified by a unique user ID and have a username, password, phone number, registration time, last login time, and role. Each user is associated with a sensor, which is a device that collects data on soil moisture, temperature, rainfall, light intensity, and other environmental factors. Sensors are linked to specific locations and are also associated with meteorological data, which includes temperature, humidity, rainfall, wind speed, and light intensity. This meteorological data is used to inform the growth of crops, which are represented by a unique crop ID, name, type, and model ID. Crop growth models are defined in the growth_model table, which contains information about the model's schema, parameters, and creation time. Users can perform operations on crops, such as watering and fertilizing, which are tracked in the user_operation table. Additionally, the system evaluates the performance of both crops and growth models, with the system_performance_evaluation and model_performance_evaluation tables storing data on evaluation metrics such as crop yields and model accuracy. The user_water_and_fertilizer_supply table tracks the supply of water and fertilizers to crops, while linking it to the associated sensor and user who performed the supply.",
  "gold_question": "Requirements:\n1.User Information: Each registered user has a unique username, password, phone number, registration time, last login time, and role. Users can supply water and fertilizer to crops through sensors, and the system needs to record the supply time, location, amount of water, and amount of fertilizer. Additionally, any other actions taken by the user on the crop (such as planting, fertilizing, etc.) need to be recorded, including the time, location, type, and details of the action. Users can also evaluate the crop’s growth performance through the system.\n2.Sensor Deployment: Sensors precisely measure meteorological data and record information such as the data collection time, soil moisture, temperature, rainfall, light intensity, sensor location, and burial depth. Each sensor can infer corresponding meteorological data.\n3.Meteorology: Each meteorological record includes timestamp, temperature, humidity, rainfall, wind speed, light intensity, and location.\n4.Crops: Each crop has a unique crop ID, name, type, and a matching growth model.\n5.Growth Model: Each crop has a corresponding growth model, which includes the model name, parameters, and creation time. The crop is evaluated using this model, and the evaluation records the name of the evaluation metric, its value, and the location of the evaluation.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0446.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0446\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sensors` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sensors_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `meteorological_data` (\n  `data_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `temperature` float NOT NULL,\n  `humidity` float NOT NULL,\n  `rainfall` float NOT NULL,\n  `wind_speed` float NOT NULL,\n  `light_intensity` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`data_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `meteorological_data_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sensor_id`) REFERENCES `sensors` (`sensor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `crops` (\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crop_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `crops_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `growth_model` (`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `growth_model` (\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `schema` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `parameters` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_operation` (\n  `operation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_operation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_operation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crops` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_performance_evaluation` (\n  `evaluation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `yield` float NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`evaluation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crops` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `model_performance_evaluation` (\n  `evaluation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `accuracy` float NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`evaluation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `model_performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `growth_model` (`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply` (\n  `supply_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supply_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crops` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`sensor_id`) REFERENCES `sensors` (`sensor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
